'' =====================================================================
''
''   File....... test-o17-setq-altd-block-ptr-delta.spin2
''   Purpose.... Hardware-verification rig deciding P2 Errata prediction O17
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 25 Sep 2026
''
'' =====================================================================

{ WHAT IS TESTED
    Prediction O17: a SETQ block RDLONG whose D field is redirected by an
    ALTD placed BETWEEN the SETQ and the RDLONG still transfers the whole
    block to the ALTD-redirected registers, but the PTRx post-update takes
    the ordinary single-transfer step (ptra++ => +4) instead of the
    block-size step (+N*4).

      setq    #N-1            ' block of N longs
      altd    idx             ' redirect rdlong's D field
      rdlong  0-0, ptra++     ' predicted: N longs land at idx, PTRA += 4

    WHAT WOULD PROVE THE PREDICTION WRONG (written before the run):
      the hazard arm advances PTRA by the same block-sized amount as its
      no-ALTD control (16 for N=4), or by any value other than 4, or the
      block does not land in full at the ALTD-redirected registers.

  RIG
    Bare P2 board (P2 Edge / EVAL).  No pins, no jumpers, no instruments.
    The measurement runs in a DEDICATED PASM cog started with COGINIT from
    the DAT block below: the Spin2 interpreter in cog 0 uses PTRA as its
    stack pointer (Spin2_interpreter.spin2 v51 :510 "wrlong v,ptra++"), so
    PTRA cannot be manipulated from cog 0.  DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001 keeps
    the debugger's interrupt out of the measuring cog (EF-057).  Cog 0
    reads the hub records and does all checking and printing.

  ARMS (run in this order, as one ROUND; NREPS = 4 rounds, interleaved)
    Before every arm the destination/trap areas are refilled with the
    sentinel $5E5E_5E5E and the pointer is reloaded, so no arm can inherit
    a previous arm's data.

    id  name      sequence                                     n  TRUE  FALSE
    --  --------  -------------------------------------------  -  ----  -----
     0  K_SINGLE  rdlong dst+2, ptra++                         1   4    (ctl)
     1  K_ALTD1   altd hidx / rdlong trp+2, ptra++              1   4    (ctl)
     2  K_BLK4    setq #3 / rdlong dst+2, ptra++                4  16    (ctl)
     3  H_BLK4    setq #3 / altd hidx / rdlong trp+2, ptra++    4   4    16   <== PRIMARY
     4  K_BLK8    setq #7 / rdlong dst+2, ptra++                8  32    (ctl)
     5  H_BLK8    setq #7 / altd hidx / rdlong trp+2, ptra++    8   4    32
     6  K_IDX1    rdlong dst+2, ptra++[3]                      1  12    (ctl)
     7  K_IDX3    setq #3 / rdlong dst+2, ptra++[3]            4  16    (ctl)
     8  H_IDX3    setq #3 / altd hidx / rdlong trp+2,ptra++[3] 4  12    16
     9  K_PTRB    setq #3 / rdlong dst+2, ptrb++               4  16    (ctl)
    10  H_PTRB    setq #3 / altd hidx / rdlong trp+2, ptrb++    4   4    16
    11  K_WR      setq #3 / wrlong wsrc+2, ptra++              4  16    (ctl)
    12  H_WR      setq #3 / altd widx / wrlong wtrp+2, ptra++   4   4    16
    13  K_Q2      setq2 #3 / rdlong LUT[2], ptra++             4  16    (ctl)
    14  H_Q2      setq2 #3 / altd lidx / rdlong LUT[18],ptra++  4   4    16

    (ctl) rows are controls: the number is the delta they MUST read.
    H rows: TRUE = PTRx delta if O17 is right; FALSE = the block delta
    (what an unaffected part does).  hidx/widx/lidx hold dst+2 / wsrc+2 /
    LUT 2, so a working ALTD sends the block to the SAME place the
    matching control uses; the H rows' literal D field points at a
    sentinel-filled TRAP area instead, so "ALTD ignored" is visible.

  WHAT EACH CONTROL PROVES
    K_SINGLE  the harness: pointer load/capture, hub source, the dump path,
              and that a plain ptra++ RDLONG steps +4 (the plain index step step)
    K_ALTD1   ALTD redirects a RDLONG's D field on this part and does not
              itself disturb the ptra++ step (+4, one long at dst+2)
    K_BLK4    = the brief's workaround (a).  The part's normal block rule:
              SETQ immediately before RDLONG => +16, 4 longs at dst+2
    K_BLK8    same at N=8 (+32), so H_BLK8 separates "one scaled unit"
              from "some fraction of the block"
    K_IDX1    a plain ptra++[3] steps +12 on this part (normal index rule)
    K_IDX3    a block ptra++[3] steps +16: the index is overridden by the
              block count (Silicon Doc v35, FAST BLOCK MOVES: "the index
              will be overridden with the number of longs")
    K_PTRB / K_WR / K_Q2   block controls for the three sibling arms
    All controls must read their delta AND full, correctly placed data in
    EVERY round, or the program prints RIG FAIL and gives no verdict for
    the arms that depend on them.  Every arm must also show the pointer-
    before value equal to the address the PASM loaded (harness check).

  DISCRIMINATORS (fixed before the run)
    PRIMARY  H_BLK4  delta TRUE = +4   FALSE = +16   (and data FULL at dst+2)
    H_BLK8   delta TRUE = +4   FALSE = +32
    H_IDX3   delta TRUE = +12  FALSE = +16  -- TRUE here is derived from
             the brief's mechanism (plain index step = the plain scaled index) plus
             the Silicon Doc's "normal PTRx expression behavior"; the brief
             itself states the value only for ptra++ (+4).  See NOTE A.
    H_PTRB / H_WR / H_Q2   TRUE = +4   FALSE = +16
    DATA half (every arm): the block region A (2 guard longs, 8 block
    slots, 2 guard longs) and the trap region B are dumped raw.
      read arms: A[2+i] must equal hub source long (RS_START+i) =
        $A5A0_0004+i for i < n; every other A slot and all of B must still
        hold the sentinel $5E5E_5E5E.
      H_WR: hub area A[2+i] must equal wsrc[2+i] = $C0C0_0002+i; B (the
        cog wtrp area) must still hold $7E7E_0000+k.  If A holds
        $7E7E_0002+i the ALTD was ignored (class TRAP).
    Data classes: FULL (exactly as predicted) / SINGLE (only the first
    long landed: SETQ lost) / TRAP (block landed at the literal D field:
    ALTD lost) / NONE (nothing landed) / OTHER.

  VERDICT RULE (per H arm, after its gates pass)
    reps disagree (delta or data class)        -> INCONCLUSIVE
    delta == TRUE  and data FULL               -> CONFIRMED
    delta == FALSE (block delta)               -> REFUTED (pointer took the block step)
    delta == TRUE  but data not FULL           -> REFUTED (pointer as predicted,
                                                  transfer not as predicted)
    any other delta                            -> REFUTED (neither value)
    The PRIMARY verdict prints last as "VERDICT: ...".  Sibling arms print
    "ARM-VERDICT <name>: ..." and do not feed the primary verdict.

  NOTE A (inferred / undetermined items this test leans on -- see brief)
    * Brief Part 2 marks as UNDETERMINED the value plain index step takes when the
      intervening instruction is ALTD.  The primary discriminator does not
      need it: TRUE=+4 comes from the brief's own Part 5 statement, and
      ANY delta other than +4 is reported as REFUTED with the raw value.
      K_SINGLE/K_ALTD1 establish that +4 is this part's ordinary ptra++
      step with and without ALTD.
    * Brief Part 2 marks as UNDETERMINED whether the ordinary step can
      coincide with the block delta; the only coincidence is N=1 (4 = 4),
      so no hazard arm uses N=1.  H_BLK8 (4 vs 32) and H_IDX3 (12 vs 16)
      move the two values apart in two independent directions.
    * H_WR, H_PTRB, H_Q2 rest on the brief's reading that block-delta path covers
      setq2 and WRLONG/WMLONG and both pointers (traced, cog.sv:1131 and
      :1124-1126); they are siblings and never gate the primary verdict.

  VERIFIED OPCODES (pnut-ts -d -l, v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read from the
  .lst hub image; cog addresses: dst=$0C6 trp=$0D2 wsrc=$0DE wtrp=$0EA
  c_hidx=$0FB c_widx=$0FC c_lidx=$0FD).  Field layout
  EEEE OOOOOOO CZI DDDDDDDDD SSSSSSSSS.
    setq  #3            $FD640628  [27:21]=1101011, D=3,  S=%000101000 (SETQ)
    setq  #7            $FD640E28  same, D=7
    setq2 #3            $FD640629  [27:21]=1101011, D=3,  S=%000101001 (SETQ2)
    altd  c_hidx        $F98DF600  [27:19]=100110001 (ALTD), I=1, D=$0FB, S=0
    altd  c_widx        $F98DF800  ALTD, D=$0FC ; altd c_lidx $F98DFA00 D=$0FD
    rdlong dst+2,ptra++ $FB059161  [27:21]=1011000 (RDLONG), I=1, D=$0C8,
                                   S=$161=%1_0_1_1_00001 = PTRA++ (S=0 PTRA,
                                   U=1 update, P=1 post, NNNNN=1)
    rdlong trp+2,ptra++ $FB05A961  RDLONG, D=$0D4 (trap), S=$161 PTRA++
    rdlong dst+2,ptra++[3] $FB059163   S=$163 = PTRA++[3]
    rdlong trp+2,ptra++[3] $FB05A963   S=$163
    rdlong dst+2,ptrb++ $FB0591E1  S=$1E1=%1_1_1_1_00001 = PTRB++
    rdlong trp+2,ptrb++ $FB05A9E1  S=$1E1
    wrlong wsrc+2,ptra++ $FC65C161 [27:21]=1100011 (WRLONG), L=0, I=1,
                                   D=$0E0, S=$161
    wrlong wtrp+2,ptra++ $FC65D961 D=$0EC, S=$161
    rdlong 2,ptra++     $FB040561  (after setq2) D=2 = LUT[2], S=$161
    rdlong 18,ptra++    $FB042561  (after setq2) D=$012 = LUT[18], S=$161
    In every H arm the three words SETQ/ALTD/RDLONG(WRLONG) are at
    consecutive hub longs (e.g. PRIMARY at image offsets $0F4/$0F8/$0FC),
    so nothing else sits between them.

  HOW TO RUN
    Load to RAM with DEBUG enabled (pnut-term-ts, or PNut Ctrl-F10 /
    "Run with DEBUG").  Runs once, well under a second; all output is on
    the DEBUG terminal.  Nothing is written to flash.  Expected output:
    a raw block of 15 arms x 4 rounds (before/after/delta/data class and
    the A and B rows), then any RIG FAIL lines, then five ARM-VERDICT
    lines, then the single PRIMARY line "VERDICT: ...".
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq      = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS    = %0000_0001            ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY (EF-057)

  NARMS         = 15
  NREPS         = 4                     ' interleaved rounds (sampling plan)
  REGN          = 12                    ' region: 2 guard + 8 block + 2 guard
  RECLEN        = 2 + 2 * REGN          ' before, after, A[12], B[12]

  SENTINEL      = $5E5E_5E5E            ' "nothing written here"
  RS_BASE       = $A5A0_0000            ' hub source long k = RS_BASE + k
  RS_START      = 4                     ' pointer starts at hub source long 4
  RS_LEN        = 48
  WS_BASE       = $C0C0_0000            ' cog wsrc[k]  = WS_BASE + k
  WT_BASE       = $7E7E_0000            ' cog wtrp[k]  = WT_BASE + k
  LUT_DST       = 0                     ' LUT region A = LUT[0..11]
  LUT_TRP       = 16                    ' LUT region B = LUT[16..27]

  STAT_RUN      = $0000_0A11
  STAT_DONE     = $0000_600D

  ' arm ids (order == run order inside one round)
  #0, A_SINGLE, A_ALTD1, A_KBLK4, A_HBLK4, A_KBLK8, A_HBLK8, A_KIDX1, A_KIDX3, A_HIDX3, A_KPTRB, A_HPTRB, A_KWR, A_HWR, A_KQ2, A_HQ2

  ' arm kinds
  #0, K_COG, K_WR, K_LUT

  ' data classes
  #0, C_FULL, C_SINGLE, C_TRAP, C_NONE, C_OTHER

  ' hazard outcomes
  #0, O_NOGATE, O_CONFIRMED, O_REF_BLOCK, O_REF_DATA, O_REF_OTHER, O_INCONCL

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long mbox[4]                          ' [0] status  [1] @hsrc  [2] @hw  [3] @rec
  long hsrc[RS_LEN]                     ' hub source block for the read arms
  long hw[REGN]                         ' hub destination area for the write arms
  long rec[NARMS * NREPS * RECLEN]      ' raw records, round-major, arm-minor
  long hok[NARMS]                       ' harness check per arm
  long stab[NARMS]                      ' reps agree per arm
  long gok[NARMS]                       ' arm reads its TRUE/expected delta + FULL data every rep
  long frep[NARMS]                      ' first rep that broke gok (-1 = none)

PUB main() | idx, cog, t0, armIdx, rigfail

  repeat idx from 0 to RS_LEN - 1
    hsrc[idx] := RS_BASE + idx
  repeat idx from 0 to REGN - 1
    hw[idx] := 0
  mbox[0] := 0
  mbox[1] := @hsrc
  mbox[2] := @hw
  mbox[3] := @rec

  debug("=== O17: SETQ + ALTD + block RDLONG PTRx delta  (pnut-ts v1.55.8, clk 200 MHz) ===")

  cog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @pasm, @mbox)
  if cog < 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: coginit expected a free cog (0..7), got ", sdec_(cog))
    finish()

  t0 := getct()
  repeat until mbox[0] == STAT_DONE
    if getct() - t0 > clkfreq
      debug("RIG FAIL: measuring cog status expected $0000_600D within 1 s, got ", uhex_long_(mbox[0]))
      finish()

  debug("measuring cog ", udec_(cog), " done. sentinel=$5E5E_5E5E  src long k=$A5A0_0000+k  ptr starts at src long 4")
  debug("RAW (A = destination region, B = trap region; slots 0,1,10,11 are guards; block at A[2..])")
  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
    report_arm(armIdx)

  ' ---- gates -------------------------------------------------------------
  rigfail := FALSE
  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
    hok[armIdx], stab[armIdx], gok[armIdx], frep[armIdx] := eval_arm(armIdx)
    if not hok[armIdx]
      rigfail := TRUE
      debug("RIG FAIL: harness, arm ", zstr_(armname(armIdx)), " pointer-before expected ", uhex_long_(startaddr(armIdx)), " in every rep; see raw rows")
    if armctl(armIdx) == -1 and not gok[armIdx]
      rigfail := TRUE
      rigfail_ctl(armIdx)
    gok[armIdx] := gok[armIdx] and hok[armIdx]         ' a control with a bad harness check gates nothing
  if not rigfail
    debug("RIG OK: every control read its expected delta and FULL data in all ", udec_(NREPS), " rounds")

  ' ---- sibling verdicts (never feed the primary) -------------------------
  debug("--- sibling arms (reported separately; do not feed the primary verdict) ---")
  print_verdict(A_HBLK8, FALSE)
  print_verdict(A_HIDX3, FALSE)
  print_verdict(A_HPTRB, FALSE)
  print_verdict(A_HWR, FALSE)
  print_verdict(A_HQ2, FALSE)

  ' ---- primary verdict ---------------------------------------------------
  debug("--- PRIMARY: H_BLK4  setq #3 / altd / rdlong 0-0, ptra++   TRUE delta +4, FALSE delta +16 ---")
  print_verdict(A_HBLK4, TRUE)

  finish()

PRI finish()
'' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
'' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' arm tables
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI armname(armIdx) : pArmName
  pArmName := lookupz(armIdx: string("K_SINGLE"), string("K_ALTD1"), string("K_BLK4"), string("H_BLK4"), string("K_BLK8"), string("H_BLK8"), string("K_IDX1"), string("K_IDX3"), string("H_IDX3"), string("K_PTRB"), string("H_PTRB"), string("K_WR"), string("H_WR"), string("K_Q2"), string("H_Q2"))

PRI armn(armIdx) : longCount            ' longs in the transfer
  longCount := lookupz(armIdx: 1, 1, 4, 4, 8, 8, 1, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4)

PRI armkind(armIdx) : kind
  kind := lookupz(armIdx: K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_COG, K_WR, K_WR, K_LUT, K_LUT)

PRI armexp(armIdx) : expDelta           ' control: required delta / hazard: delta if O17 TRUE
  expDelta := lookupz(armIdx: 4, 4, 16, 4, 32, 4, 12, 16, 12, 16, 4, 16, 4, 16, 4)

PRI armfalse(armIdx) : falseDelta       ' hazard: delta if O17 FALSE (the block delta); 0 = control
  falseDelta := lookupz(armIdx: 0, 0, 0, 16, 0, 32, 0, 0, 16, 0, 16, 0, 16, 0, 16)

PRI armctl(armIdx) : ctlArmIdx          ' hazard: its own control arm;  -1 = this arm IS a control
  ctlArmIdx := lookupz(armIdx: -1, -1, -1, A_KBLK4, -1, A_KBLK8, -1, -1, A_KIDX3, -1, A_KPTRB, -1, A_KWR, -1, A_KQ2)

PRI clsname(clsId) : pClsName
  pClsName := lookupz(clsId: string("FULL"), string("SINGLE"), string("TRAP"), string("NONE"), string("OTHER"))

PRI startaddr(armIdx) : ptrStart        ' the pointer value the PASM loads before the arm
  if armkind(armIdx) == K_WR
    ptrStart := @hw + 2 * 4
  else
    ptrStart := @hsrc + RS_START * 4

PRI recaddr(armIdx, rp) : pRec
  pRec := @rec + ((rp * NARMS + armIdx) * RECLEN) * 4

PRI aexp(armIdx, slotIdx) : expVal | longCount   ' expected A-region slot i
  longCount := armn(armIdx)
  if slotIdx < 2 or slotIdx >= 2 + longCount
    expVal := SENTINEL
  elseif armkind(armIdx) == K_WR
    expVal := WS_BASE + slotIdx
  else
    expVal := RS_BASE + RS_START + (slotIdx - 2)

PRI bexp(armIdx, slotIdx) : expVal      ' expected (untouched) B-region slot i
  if armkind(armIdx) == K_WR
    expVal := WT_BASE + slotIdx
  else
    expVal := SENTINEL

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' data classification of one record
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI classify(armIdx, rp) : cls, landed, abad, bbad | pRec, slotIdx, longCount, asent, tr
  pRec := recaddr(armIdx, rp) + 8
  longCount := armn(armIdx)
  landed := abad := bbad := asent := tr := 0
  repeat slotIdx from 0 to REGN - 1
    if long[pRec][slotIdx] <> aexp(armIdx, slotIdx)
      abad++
    if long[pRec][slotIdx] == SENTINEL
      asent++
    if long[pRec][REGN + slotIdx] <> bexp(armIdx, slotIdx)
      bbad++
  repeat slotIdx from 0 to longCount - 1
    if long[pRec][2 + slotIdx] == aexp(armIdx, 2 + slotIdx)
      landed++
    if armkind(armIdx) == K_WR
      if long[pRec][2 + slotIdx] == WT_BASE + 2 + slotIdx
        tr++
    elseif long[pRec][REGN + 2 + slotIdx] == RS_BASE + RS_START + slotIdx
      tr++
  if abad == 0 and bbad == 0
    cls := C_FULL
  elseif longCount > 1 and landed == 1 and long[pRec][2] == aexp(armIdx, 2) and asent == REGN - 1 and bbad == 0
    cls := C_SINGLE
  elseif tr == longCount
    cls := C_TRAP
  elseif asent == REGN
    cls := C_NONE
  else
    cls := C_OTHER

PRI delta(armIdx, rp) : deltaVal | pRec
  pRec := recaddr(armIdx, rp)
  deltaVal := long[pRec][1] - long[pRec][0]

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' per-arm evaluation: harness ok, reps stable, delta==armexp and FULL every rep
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI eval_arm(armIdx) : ok_h, stable, ok_g, first_bad | rp, cls, firstCls, deltaVal, firstDelta, landed, abad, bbad
  ok_h := stable := ok_g := TRUE
  first_bad := -1
  repeat rp from 0 to NREPS - 1
    if long[recaddr(armIdx, rp)][0] <> startaddr(armIdx)
      ok_h := FALSE
    cls, landed, abad, bbad := classify(armIdx, rp)
    deltaVal := delta(armIdx, rp)
    if rp == 0
      firstDelta := deltaVal
      firstCls := cls
    elseif deltaVal <> firstDelta or cls <> firstCls
      stable := FALSE
    if deltaVal <> armexp(armIdx) or cls <> C_FULL
      if ok_g
        first_bad := rp
      ok_g := FALSE

PRI rigfail_ctl(armIdx) | cls, landed, abad, bbad, rp
  rp := frep[armIdx]
  cls, landed, abad, bbad := classify(armIdx, rp)
  debug("RIG FAIL: control ", zstr_(armname(armIdx)), " expected delta ", sdec_(armexp(armIdx)), " + data FULL in every round; round ", udec_(rp), " got delta ", sdec_(delta(armIdx, rp)), " data ", zstr_(clsname(cls)), " landed ", udec_(landed), "/", udec_(armn(armIdx)))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' raw report
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI report_arm(armIdx) | rp, pRec, cls, landed, abad, bbad
  if armctl(armIdx) == -1
    debug("ARM ", udec_(armIdx), " ", zstr_(armname(armIdx)), " (control)  n=", udec_(armn(armIdx)), "  required delta=", sdec_(armexp(armIdx)))
  else
    debug("ARM ", udec_(armIdx), " ", zstr_(armname(armIdx)), " (hazard)   n=", udec_(armn(armIdx)), "  TRUE delta=", sdec_(armexp(armIdx)), "  FALSE delta=", sdec_(armfalse(armIdx)))
  repeat rp from 0 to NREPS - 1
    pRec := recaddr(armIdx, rp)
    cls, landed, abad, bbad := classify(armIdx, rp)
    debug("  round ", udec_(rp), " before=", uhex_long_(long[pRec][0]), " after=", uhex_long_(long[pRec][1]), " delta=", sdec_(long[pRec][1] - long[pRec][0]), " data=", zstr_(clsname(cls)), " landed=", udec_(landed), "/", udec_(armn(armIdx)), " abad=", udec_(abad), " bbad=", udec_(bbad))
    debug("    A: ", uhex_long_array_(pRec + 8, REGN))
    debug("    B: ", uhex_long_array_(pRec + 8 + REGN * 4, REGN))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' hazard outcome + verdict line
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI hazard_outcome(armIdx) : oc, deltaVal, cls, landed, bbad | ctl, gates, abad
  ctl := armctl(armIdx)
  gates := gok[A_SINGLE] and gok[A_ALTD1] and gok[ctl] and hok[armIdx]
  if armIdx == A_HIDX3
    gates := gates and gok[A_KIDX1]
  deltaVal := delta(armIdx, 0)
  cls, landed, abad, bbad := classify(armIdx, 0)
  if not gates
    oc := O_NOGATE
  elseif not stab[armIdx]
    oc := O_INCONCL
  elseif deltaVal == armexp(armIdx) and cls == C_FULL
    oc := O_CONFIRMED
  elseif deltaVal == armfalse(armIdx)
    oc := O_REF_BLOCK
  elseif deltaVal == armexp(armIdx)
    oc := O_REF_DATA
  else
    oc := O_REF_OTHER

PRI print_verdict(armIdx, primary) | oc, deltaVal, cls, landed, bbad, pfx
  oc, deltaVal, cls, landed, bbad := hazard_outcome(armIdx)
  if primary
    pfx := string("VERDICT")
  else
    pfx := lookupz(armIdx: 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, string("ARM-VERDICT H_BLK8"), 0, 0, string("ARM-VERDICT H_IDX3"), 0, string("ARM-VERDICT H_PTRB"), 0, string("ARM-VERDICT H_WR"), 0, string("ARM-VERDICT H_Q2"))
  case oc
    O_NOGATE:
      debug("NO VERDICT for ", zstr_(armname(armIdx)), ": a gating control or the harness check failed - see RIG FAIL lines")
    O_INCONCL:
      debug(zstr_(pfx), ": INCONCLUSIVE - the ", udec_(NREPS), " rounds disagree (delta or data class); see raw rows for ", zstr_(armname(armIdx)))
    O_CONFIRMED:
      debug(zstr_(pfx), ": CONFIRMED - pointer delta ", sdec_(deltaVal), " (TRUE value) while all ", udec_(armn(armIdx)), " longs landed at the ALTD destination, in all ", udec_(NREPS), " rounds; control delta ", sdec_(armfalse(armIdx)))
    O_REF_BLOCK:
      debug(zstr_(pfx), ": REFUTED - pointer took the BLOCK delta ", sdec_(deltaVal), " (FALSE value) despite the ALTD; data=", zstr_(clsname(cls)), " landed ", udec_(landed), "/", udec_(armn(armIdx)), " trap-slots-changed ", udec_(bbad))
    O_REF_DATA:
      debug(zstr_(pfx), ": REFUTED - pointer delta ", sdec_(deltaVal), " as predicted, but the block did NOT transfer as predicted: data=", zstr_(clsname(cls)), " landed ", udec_(landed), "/", udec_(armn(armIdx)), " trap-slots-changed ", udec_(bbad))
    O_REF_OTHER:
      debug(zstr_(pfx), ": REFUTED - pointer delta ", sdec_(deltaVal), " is neither TRUE ", sdec_(armexp(armIdx)), " nor FALSE ", sdec_(armfalse(armIdx)), "; data=", zstr_(clsname(cls)), " landed ", udec_(landed), "/", udec_(armn(armIdx)))

' ===========================================================================
' MEASURING COG (PASM, cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox (from COGINIT).
' No debug() in here: this cog has no debug interrupt (DEBUG_COGS).
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Cog ----
pasm            mov     c_mbx, ptra                     ' save @mbox before PTRA is used
                mov     c_t, c_mbx
                add     c_t, #4
                rdlong  c_rsrc, c_t                     ' @hsrc
                add     c_rsrc, #RS_START * 4           ' read arms start at src long 4
                add     c_t, #4
                rdlong  c_hwbase, c_t                   ' @hw
                mov     c_hwst, c_hwbase
                add     c_hwst, #2 * 4                  ' write arms start after 2 guard longs
                add     c_t, #4
                rdlong  c_recp, c_t                     ' @rec
                mov     c_hidx, #dst + 2                ' ALTD targets: the SAME place the
                mov     c_widx, #wsrc + 2               '  matching control uses
                mov     c_lidx, #LUT_DST + 2
                mov     c_t, ##STAT_RUN
                wrlong  c_t, c_mbx
                mov     c_rnd, #NREPS

one_round
'--- arm 0  K_SINGLE : plain rdlong, ptra++ (ordinary step)
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                rdlong  dst + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 1  K_ALTD1 : ALTD-redirected single rdlong, ptra++
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                altd    c_hidx
                rdlong  trp + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 2  K_BLK4 : workaround (a) -- SETQ immediately before RDLONG
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq    #4 - 1
                rdlong  dst + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 3  H_BLK4 : PRIMARY hazard -- SETQ / ALTD / RDLONG ptra++
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq    #4 - 1
                altd    c_hidx
                rdlong  trp + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 4  K_BLK8
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq    #8 - 1
                rdlong  dst + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 5  H_BLK8
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq    #8 - 1
                altd    c_hidx
                rdlong  trp + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 6  K_IDX1 : plain rdlong, ptra++[3] (ordinary step = 3*4)
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                rdlong  dst + 2, ptra++[3]
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 7  K_IDX3 : block rdlong, ptra++[3] (index overridden by count)
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq    #4 - 1
                rdlong  dst + 2, ptra++[3]
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 8  H_IDX3
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq    #4 - 1
                altd    c_hidx
                rdlong  trp + 2, ptra++[3]
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 9  K_PTRB
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptrb, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptrb
                setq    #4 - 1
                rdlong  dst + 2, ptrb++
                mov     c_after, ptrb
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 10 H_PTRB
                call    #prep_cog
                mov     ptrb, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptrb
                setq    #4 - 1
                altd    c_hidx
                rdlong  trp + 2, ptrb++
                mov     c_after, ptrb
                call    #dump_cog
'--- arm 11 K_WR : block wrlong from cog wsrc[2..5] to hub
                call    #prep_wr
                mov     ptra, c_hwst
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq    #4 - 1
                wrlong  wsrc + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_wr
'--- arm 12 H_WR
                call    #prep_wr
                mov     ptra, c_hwst
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq    #4 - 1
                altd    c_widx
                wrlong  wtrp + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_wr
'--- arm 13 K_Q2 : setq2 block rdlong into LUT[2..5]
                call    #prep_lut
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq2   #4 - 1
                rdlong  LUT_DST + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_lut
'--- arm 14 H_Q2
                call    #prep_lut
                mov     ptra, c_rsrc
                mov     c_before, ptra
                setq2   #4 - 1
                altd    c_lidx
                rdlong  LUT_TRP + 2, ptra++
                mov     c_after, ptra
                call    #dump_lut

                djnz    c_rnd, #one_round
                mov     c_t, ##STAT_DONE
                wrlong  c_t, c_mbx
                cogid   c_t
                cogstop c_t

'--- fill cog dst[] and trp[] (contiguous, 2*REGN longs) with the sentinel
prep_cog        mov     c_i, #0
.lp             altd    c_i, #dst
                mov     0-0, c_sent
                add     c_i, #1
                cmp     c_i, #2 * REGN          wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.lp
                ret

'--- fill the hub write area (REGN longs) with the sentinel
prep_wr         mov     c_p, c_hwbase
                mov     c_i, #REGN
.lp             wrlong  c_sent, c_p
                add     c_p, #4
                djnz    c_i, #.lp
                ret

'--- fill LUT[0..LUT_TRP+REGN-1] with the sentinel
prep_lut        mov     c_i, #0
.lp             wrlut   c_sent, c_i
                add     c_i, #1
                cmp     c_i, #LUT_TRP + REGN    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.lp
                ret

'--- record header: before, after
dump_hdr        wrlong  c_before, c_recp
                add     c_recp, #4
                wrlong  c_after, c_recp
        _ret_   add     c_recp, #4

'--- record: header, A = cog dst[0..11], B = cog trp[0..11]
dump_cog        call    #dump_hdr
                mov     c_i, #0
.lp             altd    c_i, #dst
                wrlong  0-0, c_recp
                add     c_recp, #4
                add     c_i, #1
                cmp     c_i, #2 * REGN          wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.lp
                ret

'--- record: header, A = hub write area[0..11], B = cog wtrp[0..11]
dump_wr         call    #dump_hdr
                mov     c_p, c_hwbase
                mov     c_i, #REGN
.a              rdlong  c_t, c_p
                wrlong  c_t, c_recp
                add     c_p, #4
                add     c_recp, #4
                djnz    c_i, #.a
                mov     c_i, #0
.b              altd    c_i, #wtrp
                wrlong  0-0, c_recp
                add     c_recp, #4
                add     c_i, #1
                cmp     c_i, #REGN              wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.b
                ret

'--- record: header, A = LUT[0..11], B = LUT[16..27]
dump_lut        call    #dump_hdr
                mov     c_i, #LUT_DST
.a              rdlut   c_t, c_i
                wrlong  c_t, c_recp
                add     c_recp, #4
                add     c_i, #1
                cmp     c_i, #LUT_DST + REGN    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.a
                mov     c_i, #LUT_TRP
.b              rdlut   c_t, c_i
                wrlong  c_t, c_recp
                add     c_recp, #4
                add     c_i, #1
                cmp     c_i, #LUT_TRP + REGN    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.b
                ret

'--- cog data
c_sent          long    SENTINEL
dst             long    0[REGN]                         ' region A for cog read arms
trp             long    0[REGN]                         ' region B (trap) -- MUST follow dst
wsrc            long    WS_BASE + 0, WS_BASE + 1, WS_BASE + 2,  WS_BASE + 3
                long    WS_BASE + 4, WS_BASE + 5, WS_BASE + 6,  WS_BASE + 7
                long    WS_BASE + 8, WS_BASE + 9, WS_BASE + 10, WS_BASE + 11
wtrp            long    WT_BASE + 0, WT_BASE + 1, WT_BASE + 2,  WT_BASE + 3
                long    WT_BASE + 4, WT_BASE + 5, WT_BASE + 6,  WT_BASE + 7
                long    WT_BASE + 8, WT_BASE + 9, WT_BASE + 10, WT_BASE + 11
c_mbx           long    0
c_rsrc          long    0
c_hwbase        long    0
c_hwst          long    0
c_recp          long    0
c_hidx          long    0
c_widx          long    0
c_lidx          long    0
c_rnd           long    0
c_i             long    0
c_t             long    0
c_p             long    0
c_before        long    0
c_after         long    0

